   "name": "COMP.asc",
   "kind": "schematic",
   "text": "Version 4\r\nSHEET 1 1000 700\r\nWIRE 32 0 32 -16\r\nWIRE 80 16 112 16\r\nWIRE 32 96 32 128\r\nWIRE 32 128 32 160\r\nWIRE 32 240 32 256\r\nWIRE 320 0 320 -16\r\nWIRE 272 16 240 16\r\nWIRE 320 96 320 176\r\nWIRE 224 176 320 176\r\nWIRE 320 176 416 176\r\nWIRE 176 192 128 192\r\nWIRE 464 192 512 192\r\nWIRE 224 272 224 320\r\nWIRE 224 320 224 368\r\nWIRE 224 320 320 320\r\nWIRE 320 320 320 448\r\nWIRE 272 448 320 448\r\nWIRE 320 448 368 448\r\nWIRE 224 464 224 480\r\nWIRE 416 464 416 480\r\nWIRE 416 272 416 320\r\nWIRE 416 320 416 368\r\nWIRE 416 320 560 320\r\nWIRE 608 336 608 352\r\nWIRE 608 0 608 -16\r\nWIRE 560 16 528 16\r\nWIRE 608 96 608 176\r\nWIRE 608 176 608 240\r\nWIRE 800 0 800 -16\r\nWIRE 608 176 704 176\r\nWIRE 752 16 704 16\r\nWIRE 704 16 704 176\r\nWIRE 704 176 704 320\r\nWIRE 704 320 752 320\r\nWIRE 800 96 800 176\r\nWIRE 800 176 800 240\r\nWIRE 800 176 864 176\r\nWIRE 800 336 800 352\r\nFLAG 32 -16 vdd\r\nIOPIN 32 -16 In\r\nFLAG 112 16 bias\r\nFLAG 32 128 bias\r\nFLAG 32 256 0\r\nFLAG 320 -16 vdd\r\nFLAG 240 16 bias\r\nFLAG 128 192 inp\r\nIOPIN 128 192 In\r\nFLAG 512 192 inn\r\nIOPIN 512 192 In\r\nFLAG 224 480 0\r\nFLAG 416 480 0\r\nFLAG 608 352 0\r\nFLAG 608 -16 vdd\r\nFLAG 528 16 bias\r\nFLAG 800 -16 vdd\r\nFLAG 864 176 out\r\nIOPIN 864 176 Out\r\nFLAG 800 352 0\r\nSYMBOL pmos 80 96 R180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M8\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=10u\r\nSYMBOL res 16 144 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName Rb\r\nSYMATTR Value 180k\r\nSYMBOL pmos 272 96 M180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M5\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=20u\r\nSYMBOL pmos 176 272 M180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M1\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=20u\r\nSYMBOL pmos 464 272 R180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M2\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=20u\r\nSYMBOL nmos 272 368 M0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M3\r\nSYMATTR Value NM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=5u\r\nSYMBOL nmos 368 368 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M4\r\nSYMATTR Value NM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=5u\r\nSYMBOL nmos 560 240 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M6\r\nSYMATTR Value NM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=10u\r\nSYMBOL pmos 560 96 M180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M7\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=20u\r\nSYMBOL pmos 752 96 M180\r\nSYMATTR InstName M9\r\nSYMATTR Value PM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=4u\r\nSYMBOL nmos 752 240 R0\r\nSYMATTR InstName M10\r\nSYMATTR Value NM\r\nSYMATTR Value2 l=1u w=2u\r\nTEXT 64 -176 Left 2 ;Comparator of the SAR ADC: out = vdd when inp > inn, 0 when inp < inn.\\nM1-M2 (PMOS pair) with the M3-M4 mirror, M6 common source and the M9-M10 inverter: a gain of about 40 000,\\nenough to resolve much less than 1 LSB (19.5 mV) in a fraction of the 1 µs clock cycle.\\nM8 and Rb set the bias current (about 20 µA) that M5 (tail, 2×) and M7 (2×) copy.\r\nTEXT 64 576 Left 2 !.model NM NMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=0.7 KP=110u LAMBDA=0.04 TOX=10n CGSO=0.3n CGDO=0.3n CJ=0.5m)\r\nTEXT 64 608 Left 2 !.model PM PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.7 KP=50u LAMBDA=0.05 TOX=10n CGSO=0.3n CGDO=0.3n CJ=0.5m)\r\n"
  },
  {
   "name": "COMP.asy",
   "kind": "symbol",
   "text": "Version 4\nSymbolType BLOCK\nLINE Normal -64 -64 64 0\nLINE Normal 64 0 -64 64\nLINE Normal -64 64 -64 -64\nLINE Normal -56 -32 -40 -32\nLINE Normal -48 -40 -48 -24\nLINE Normal -56 32 -40 32\nLINE Normal 0 -32 0 -64\nLINE Normal -28 12 -12 12\nLINE Normal -12 12 -12 -12\nLINE Normal -12 -12 4 -12\nWINDOW 0 8 -40 Left 2\nSYMATTR Prefix X\nSYMATTR Description CMOS comparator of the project: PMOS differential pair, common-source stage and an output inverter\nPIN -64 -32 NONE 8\nPINATTR PinName inp\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 1\nPIN -64 32 NONE 8\nPINATTR PinName inn\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 2\nPIN 64 0 NONE 8\nPINATTR PinName out\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 3\nPIN 0 -64 NONE 8\nPINATTR PinName vdd\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 4\n"
  },
  {
   "name": "ASW.lib",
   "kind": "model",
   "module": "model",
   "text": "* ASW: analog switch of the ADC project, made with the XSPICE aswitch.\n* Between Vc = 1 V (open, roff) and Vc = 4 V (closed, ron) the resistance changes smoothly\n* (logarithmically): with the abrupt SPICE switch (S) and the digital bridges of the Verilog\n* blocks switching at the same time, ngspice cannot find the time step.\n.subckt ASW n1 n2 c+ c- params: ron=100 roff=1g\nA1 %vd(c+ c-) %gd(n1 n2) aswm\n.model aswm aswitch(cntl_off=1 cntl_on=4 r_off={roff} r_on={ron} log=TRUE)\n.ends ASW\n"
  },
  {
   "name": "ASW.asy",
   "kind": "symbol",
   "text": "Version 4\nSymbolType CELL\nLINE Normal 0 40 0 24\nLINE Normal 0 88 0 73\nLINE Normal 17 67 0 40\nLINE Normal -48 32 -32 32\nLINE Normal -32 32 -23 37\nLINE Normal -48 80 -32 80\nLINE Normal -32 80 -23 75\nLINE Normal 0 16 0 24\nLINE Normal 0 96 0 88\nLINE Normal -44 45 -44 39\nLINE Normal -47 42 -41 42\nLINE Normal 8 56 -21 56 2\nCIRCLE Normal -32 24 32 88\nWINDOW 0 40 40 Left 2\nWINDOW 39 40 72 Left 0\nSYMATTR Prefix X\nSYMATTR SpiceModel ASW\nSYMATTR ModelFile ASW.lib\nSYMATTR SpiceLine ron=100 roff=1g\nSYMATTR Description Analog switch (XSPICE aswitch) of the project: closed when V(Vc+, Vc-) > 4 V, open below 1 V\nPIN 0 16 NONE 0\nPINATTR PinName Sw1\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 1\nPIN 0 96 NONE 0\nPINATTR PinName Sw2\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 2\nPIN -48 32 NONE 0\nPINATTR PinName Vc+\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 3\nPIN -48 80 NONE 0\nPINATTR PinName Vc-\nPINATTR SpiceOrder 4\n\n"
  }
