 bot[3]\nFLAG 608 320 bot[2]\nFLAG 704 320 bot[1]\nFLAG 800 320 bot[0]\nFLAG 896 320 0\nFLAG 512 128 top\nFLAG 96 672 vin\nFLAG 16 576 smp\nFLAG 48 640 0\nFLAG 384 672 vref\nFLAG 384 464 bot[7:0]\nFLAG 304 576 up[7:0]\nFLAG 336 640 0\nFLAG 672 672 0\nFLAG 592 576 dn[7:0]\nFLAG 624 640 0\nFLAG 960 528 top\nFLAG 960 672 vcm\nFLAG 880 576 smp\nFLAG 912 640 0\nFLAG 1104 128 vcm\nFLAG 1216 64 vdd\nFLAG 1328 160 cmp\nFLAG 1344 848 data[7:0]\nFLAG 1344 1024 dac,n[6:0]\nFLAG 1504 848 dac,n[6:1]\nFLAG 1504 1024 n[6:0]\nFLAG 1664 848 n[0]\nFLAG 1664 1024 0\nFLAG 1360 512 clk\nFLAG 1360 544 cmp\nFLAG 1552 512 smp\nFLAG 1552 544 up[7:0]\nFLAG 1552 576 dn[7:0]\nFLAG 1552 608 eoc\nFLAG 1552 640 data[7:0]\nSYMBOL voltage 64 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Vin\nSYMATTR Value 3.1\nSYMBOL voltage 224 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Vref\nSYMATTR Value 5\nSYMBOL voltage 384 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Vcm\nSYMATTR Value 2.5\nSYMBOL voltage 544 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Vdd\nSYMATTR Value 5\nSYMBOL voltage 704 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Vclk\nSYMATTR Value PULSE(0 5 0.5u 5n 5n 495n 1u)\nSYMBOL cap 112 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C7\nSYMATTR Value {128*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 208 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C6\nSYMATTR Value {64*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 304 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C5\nSYMATTR Value {32*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 400 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C4\nSYMATTR Value {16*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 496 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C3\nSYMATTR Value {8*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 592 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C2\nSYMATTR Value {4*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 688 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C1\nSYMATTR Value {2*Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 784 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName C0\nSYMATTR Value {Cu}\nSYMBOL cap 880 224 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Cd\nSYMATTR Value {Cu}\nSYMBOL ASW 96 544 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Ssmp[7:0]\nSYMBOL ASW 384 544 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Sref[7:0]\nSYMBOL ASW 672 544 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Sgnd[7:0]\nSYMBOL ASW 960 544 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Stop\nSYMBOL COMP 1216 160 R0\nSYMATTR InstName X1\nSYMBOL SARLOGIC 1456 576 R0\nSYMATTR InstName X2\nSYMBOL res 1328 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Rb[7:0]\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 1488 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Rs[6:0]\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 1648 880 R0\nSYMATTR InstName Rt\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nTEXT 112 -144 Left 2 ;8-bit SAR ADC with charge redistribution. One conversion takes 10 clock cycles, in three phases that never overlap:\\n1) Sample (smp = 1): Stop puts the top plate on vcm and Ssmp the bottom plates of the binary array (C7 = 128 Cu … C0 = Cu) on vin.\\n2) Hold (every switch open): the floating top plate keeps that charge, which is the sample.\\n3) Eight trials: Sref and Sgnd put each bottom plate on vref (up[k], the bits at 1 of the code being tried) or on ground (dn[k]): then top = vcm − vin·255/256 + vref·code/256.\\nThe comparator (COMP, a CMOS subcircuit of the project) says whether top is below vcm, that is, whether vin is above the trial voltage,\\nand SARLOGIC.v keeps or drops each bit, MSB first. Result: data = vin·255/vref, once every 10 clock cycles (100 kS/s at 1 MHz).\\nThe switches (ASW) are a «Model» module of the project: the XSPICE analog switch, which changes its resistance smoothly.\nTEXT 1296 768 Left 2 ;R-2R DAC, only to see data as a voltage:\\ndac = 5 V · data / 256\nTEXT 64 928 Left 2 !.param Cu=100f\nTEXT 64 960 Left 2 !.tran 21u\nTEXT 54 720 Left 2 ;Input Switches\n",
