TTR InstName R11\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 456 784 R90\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\nSYMATTR InstName R21\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 464 704 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R12\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 616 784 R90\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\nSYMATTR InstName R22\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 624 704 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R13\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 776 784 R90\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\nSYMATTR InstName R23\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 784 704 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R14\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 936 784 R90\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\nSYMATTR InstName R24\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 944 704 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R15\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 1096 784 R90\nWINDOW 0 0 56 VBottom 2\nWINDOW 3 32 56 VTop 2\nSYMATTR InstName R25\nSYMATTR Value 10k\nSYMBOL res 1104 704 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R16\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nSYMBOL res 144 800 R0\nSYMATTR InstName R30\nSYMATTR Value 20k\nTEXT 96 -96 Left 2 ;First-order sigma-delta ADC in two Verilog blocks. Modulator: R1 carries the current of Vin and R2 the one of the feedback fb into node «int», and C1 integrates them;\\nMODULATOR (the 1-bit quantizer) compares «int» with vcc/2 on each clock edge: above it, y = 1 and fb goes to 0 and discharges C1; below it, y = 0 and fb goes to 1 and charges it.\\nSo «int» stays near 2.5 V, the average of fb follows 5 V − Vin and the fraction of ones in the stream y is Vin / 5 V. DOWNSAMPLER turns that 1 MHz stream into 7-bit words.\nTEXT 1008 416 Left 2 ;DOWNSAMPLER: every 64 clock cycles it puts on the bus d[6:0]\\nhow many ones came in on y (0 … 64): 15.6 kS/s.\nTEXT 160 624 Left 2 ;7-bit R-2R DAC: each bit of the bus d[6:0] goes in through a 20k; out = 5 V · code / 128 ≈ Vin/2\nTEXT 160 1008 Left 2 !.tran 8m\n"
